// ---- A tear running through a fibrous sheet, macro, with the camera tracking the tip.
// The sheet scrolls past a tear tip that stays put, so the tear NEVER finishes — the piece is
// perpetual by construction, no reset, no convergence.
// The real mechanics: ahead of the tip a process zone whitens under stress; at the tip the mat
// separates along one ragged path so the two deckle edges INTERLOCK (they were one edge);
// behind it the flaps pull apart and single fibres BRIDGE the gap — going slack, then taut,
// then snapping and recoiling as dangling pull-out. That bridging zone is what makes paper tough.
